depgraph: put the merge order calculation off in attempts that restart

Sub-series: P (stage 5) - patch 2 of 3; applies without 0035 and 0037, in any order with them.
Base: upstream bdf046b03 with 0001-0034.

_resolve() asks altlist() for the merge list before its tests for a restart,
and in most backtracking attempts the list is thrown away with the depgraph.
altlist() now puts _serialize_tasks() off when a graph test
(_stage5_serialize_cannot_fail) shows that the node selection loop cannot end
in its "no node selected" branch, the only place where _serialize_tasks()
writes backtracking state; also required: no uninstall tasks, no blocker
uninstalls, no pending cycle break, no --debug. The list is computed as soon
as the depgraph is kept or anybody asks for it (_stage5_finish_serialize). The
argument is written out in the docstring of _stage5_serialize_skippable().

Lock-step check: _stage5_verify_serialize_skip (PORTAGE_STAGE5_VERIFY=1 or
"serialize") carries out every calculation that would be put off, on the spot,
and raises AssertionError unless it ends as predicted, leaves the backtracking
state alone and equals the list computed later. New test:
tests/resolver/test_serialize_deferral.py (covers the combination with 0035
when that patch is applied too).

Six-state sum, stage 5 judge, on top of 0035: 76.6 -> 74.2 s (about 3 %). Alone
beside the unchanged series on 2026-11-24: 88.8 -> 87.2 s and 90.6 -> 92.7 s,
i.e. within the noise of that host; the gain shows with 0035, whose reused
attempts keep a list that was put off. Lock-step run on the six states: no
difference.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, stage 5, 2026-11-24
(two rounds of implementer agents, black-box tester agents and a timing judge);
split into independent patches and re-checked on 2026-11-24. Not a human-written
change. Base: upstream bdf046b03 with patches 0001-0034. Test: `emerge -p -uND
@world` on six states of one system image, six resolves in parallel; every run
gave the same merge list in order and the same number of backtracking attempts
as unpatched bdf046b03.

